  <main class="detail-main" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/journal/">Journal</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Should a silver filling be replaced? Start with the reason.</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Materials · 4 min read</p><h1>Should a silver filling be replaced? Start with the reason.</h1><p class="detail-lead">A conversation about an existing amalgam filling should start with the condition of the tooth and the reason for considering replacement.</p></div></div><div class="wrap detail-grid"><article class="detail-card prose"><p class="editorial-note" data-editorial-review>Staging only — this article is hidden from the public site until clinically approved in the Raina Website settings.</p><section><h2>Look at the existing filling</h2><p>Ask your dentist to explain what the exam shows and whether there is a clinical reason to replace the filling. The FDA generally advises against removing intact amalgam fillings unless removal is medically necessary. Removing one can take away healthy tooth structure and temporarily increase exposure to mercury vapor.</p></section><section><h2>Understand when SMART enters the conversation</h2><p>SMART stands for Safe Mercury Amalgam Removal Technique. It is a protocol developed by the International Academy of Oral Medicine and Toxicology for use when removal is undertaken. Ask which precautions the office uses and why. The reason for replacing a filling and the way it is removed are separate decisions.</p></section><section><h2>Discuss the next restoration</h2><p>If the dentist recommends a new restoration, ask which materials suit the location and condition of the tooth, how much tooth structure is involved and what maintenance would look like. It can help to write down what you want to understand before the visit.</p></section><h2>Further reading</h2><ul><li><a class="text-link" href="https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/dental-amalgam-fillings/information-patients-about-dental-amalgam-fillings">FDA · Dental amalgam fillings <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></li><li><a class="text-link" href="https://iaomt.org/resources/safe-removal-amalgam-fillings/">IAOMT · SMART protocol <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/care/smart/">Explore SMART amalgam removal <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></article><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="aside-mark" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p class="eyebrow">Raina Dental Care</p><h2>Let’s talk.</h2><p>2323 Naperville Road, Suite 110<br>Naperville, Illinois</p><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Schedule a visit <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call (630) 381-4021 <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></aside></div></main>
